        description: "Advanced Practitioner\n\nSuzanne Albert is a Family Nurse Practitioner at Austin Area OB/GYN and Fertility who has been in practice for more than 20 years; including over 18 years of women’s health provision. She is able to see patients for comprehensive care including: routine OB patients, annual well woman exams, IUDs, Nexplanons, postmenopausal bleeding, colposcopies, irregular bleeding, depression, vaginitis, breast problems, postpartum depression, and mastitis.\n\nSuzanne graduated cum laude from D’Youville College with a Bachelor of Science in Nursing and then magna cum laude from the State University of New York at Buffalo with a Master’s of Science in Nursing as a Family Nurse Practitioner. A native of Buffalo, New York, she moved to Austin, Texas in 1999 for her husband’s new job and quickly fell in love with Texas and Austin in particular. She and her husband have 2 sons and a sweet dog that keep them busy with their sports, volunteering, and social life in general. She enjoys spending time with friends, cooking, volunteering at school and temple, exercising and her book club.",
        photoUrl: "https://aaobgyn.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Suzanne-Albert-FNP-BC.png",
